1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,443
Stop losing hours to manual spreadsheet cleanups.

2
00:00:03,443 --> 00:00:13,491
A typical export with mixed country names, duplicate IDs, and broken dates breaks VLOOKUPs fast—and zeroing out dashes silently corrupts revenue.

3
00:00:13,491 --> 00:00:18,120
In two minutes, let's replace all of that with a verified ten-second pipeline.

4
00:00:18,470 --> 00:00:20,472
Look at what needs to happen row by row.

5
00:00:20,472 --> 00:00:32,436
Duplicate customer rows get audited and dropped, aliases like U-S-A and Deutschland map cleanly to canonical names, and missing spend dashes become NaN—never silent zeros.

6
00:00:32,786 --> 00:00:37,429
Never ask an AI prompt to blindly edit a spreadsheet in one shot.

7
00:00:37,429 --> 00:00:49,128
Split it into three strict stages: Parse and audit raw anomalies first, normalize deterministically with clear guardrails second, and validate every column with assertions third.

8
00:00:49,478 --> 00:00:55,525
First inside cleaner dot py, we remove duplicate customer records keeping the first occurrence.

9
00:00:55,525 --> 00:01:03,804
Next, we replace dashes and N-A markers with N-A-N before numeric coercion so missing numbers never poison revenue averages.

10
00:01:04,154 --> 00:01:10,059
For messy dates, pandas mixed format parses ISO and slash timestamps in one line.

11
00:01:10,059 --> 00:01:17,112
And for country cleanup, any value missing from the mapping dictionary is kept intact rather than dropped silently.

12
00:01:17,462 --> 00:01:29,652
When you execute the pipeline, it emits a step-by-step audit trail and checks five strict assertions: unique IDs, numeric spend, valid dates, canonical countries, and row-count sanity.

13
00:01:30,002 --> 00:01:41,400
Across our messy export, forty noisy rows become twenty verified clean records in seconds—with twenty duplicates caught, seven nulls preserved, and all five schema checks green.

14
00:01:41,750 --> 00:01:47,808
The complete script, messy sample dataset, and verification report are live on GitHub right now.

15
00:01:47,808 --> 00:01:53,340
